BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:02dfe6e732b2f0563255de4c6849920b@mdh
DTSTAMP:20261015T153406Z
DTSTART:20261016T210000Z
DTEND:20261016T215000Z
SUMMARY:🏒 Drop-In/Pickup – Sylvania\, OH
DESCRIPTION:The Buckeye Broadband Hockey League (BBHL) is sponsored by Buckeye Broadband. Players receive a Buckeye Broadband game jersey\, game sox\, and five (5) Toledo Walleye game vouchers. Regular season runs late-September thru mid-March. The majority of the ice touches will be at Sylvania Tam-O-Shanter. There will be a ice touches at Ottawa Park and one ice time at the Huntington Center. RATE SKATE: All players are required to attend a rate skate in September. The rate skate is NOT a tryout for the BBHL. All registered players will be placed on a team. ICE TIMES: Teams will skate 1-3 times per week (practices and games). The weekly schedule will vary. Each team will receive approximately 35-38 ice times. The schedule will be available online once the season begins. ALL-STARS: From the BBHL\, one all-star team will be formed at each the 10U\, 12U\, &amp\; 14U levels. There are separate tryouts for the Maple Leafs All-Star teams. Please refer to tamohockey.com for more information regarding the Maple Leafs program. GIRLS: Girls hockey is a priority for the club. The BBHL assembles a girls only team at the 8U level each season. Girls ages 6-9 years may be considered to assemble this girls only team. The team is placed in the BBHL for practice and game purposes. PLAYING FORMAT: 6U &amp\; 8U will practice in a station based format following the USA Hockey American Development Model. 6U games will be played cross-ice. 8U games will be played half-ice. 10U-14U will practice half-ice and play full-ice games.&nbsp\; USA HOCKEY MEMBERSHIP: All players are required to register annually with USA Hockey for the existing playing season. Online registration can be completed at usahockey.com. TOLEDO WALLEYE VOUCHER FUNDRAISER: Each registered player will receive five (5) Toledo Walleye game vouchers. The cost of the vouchers is included in the BBHL player fee. Families may use their vouchers or re-sell them at face value.&nbsp\; COACHES: Head and assistant coaches are wanted. Please indicate your interest level during the online registration process. CARPOOLS: The BBHL cannot guarantee carpool requests will be granted in the fall/winter session. There is more flexibility with carpool requests in the spring session. BBHL DIRECTOR: Questions and concerns may be directed to mmanko@sylvaniatamoshanter.com.\nRink: Tam-O-Shanter Ice Rink – Sylvania\, OH\n~58 mi from Ann Arbor\nPrice: $10\nSource: DaySmart\nInfo: https://apps.daysmartrecreation.com/dash/x/#/online/tamoshanter/event-registration\nConfirm with rink — schedule subject to change.
LOCATION:Tam-O-Shanter Ice Rink – Sylvania\, OH
URL:https://apps.daysmartrecreation.com/dash/x/#/online/tamoshanter/event-registration
END:VEVENT
